From fac04b1423f5d3ad85afa17b768b9ce5cf043cf3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moWerk <mo@mowerk.net>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:04:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] tee: qseecom: Copy the request back when the client marks
 it INOUT
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Android's QSEECom_send_cmd() takes separate request and response
pointers, and clients may pass the same buffer for both. Trusted
applications written against such a client answer in place, over the
request: the Pro1X fingerprint application (mafp) does, and with the
request staged in kernel memory and only the response area copied out,
every reply it gave was lost.

qseecom_tee_memref() already accepts an INOUT memref for the request.
Give that marking a meaning: when the request parameter is INOUT, copy
the staged request back to the client after the send, so the client sees
what the application wrote there. INPUT requests are left untouched.

Replaces the unconditional test copy of 2026-11-09 (w-73 e547c793b).

Disclosure: LLMGD-2 · origin O1 (the model wrote it; the author tested the behaviour on the device and can verify that, not the code)
LLMGD: v0.3; assurance=A2; flags=T; origin=O1; origin_headline=O1; scope=kernel; graded-by=claude-fable-5-1; retrieval=none
---
 drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c b/drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c
index da6ac5fd6..01d4d3b1a 100644
--- a/drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c
+++ b/drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c
@@ -800,7 +800,7 @@ static int qseecom_tee_invoke_func(struct tee_context *ctx,
 	struct qseecom_tee_session *sess;
 	size_t req_size, rsp_size;
 	u32 app_gen;
-	bool found;
+	bool found, req_inout;
 	void *req, *rsp;
 	unsigned int i;
 	u32 app_id;
@@ -840,6 +840,8 @@ static int qseecom_tee_invoke_func(struct tee_context *ctx,
 				 &req, &req_size);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
+	req_inout = (param[0].attr & TEE_IOCTL_PARAM_ATTR_TYPE_MASK) ==
+		    TEE_IOCTL_PARAM_ATTR_TYPE_MEMREF_INOUT;
 
 	ret = qseecom_tee_memref(&param[1], TEE_IOCTL_PARAM_ATTR_TYPE_MEMREF_OUTPUT,
 				 &rsp, &rsp_size);
@@ -954,6 +956,16 @@ static int qseecom_tee_invoke_func(struct tee_context *ctx,
 		if (!ret) {
 			memcpy(rsp, b + req_size, rsp_size);
 
+			/*
+			 * Android's QSEECom_send_cmd() lets a client pass one
+			 * buffer as both request and response, and trusted
+			 * applications written against that answer in place,
+			 * over the request. A client that marks the request
+			 * INOUT asks for what the application left there.
+			 */
+			if (req_inout)
+				memcpy(req, b, req_size);
+
 			off = PAGE_ALIGN(req_size + rsp_size);
 			for (k = 2; k < arg->num_params; k += 2) {
 				struct tee_shm *pshm = param[k + 1].u.memref.shm;
-- 
